<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Amalia posts Q2 net loss.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Amalia posts Q2 net loss.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-June versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss for period	   4.86  vs  4.45</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled		  15.99  vs  2.20</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)	     12     vs  nil</p>
<p>    Cost (rand/tonne)	   237.96  vs 341.50</p>
<p>    Total income		    1.13  vs  0.82 loss</p>
<p>Full name: Amalia Gold Mining and Exploration Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said significant once-off restructuring costs had been incurred and cost reductions would be apparent over the next two quarters.</p>
<p>Mining in better grade areas had alread resulted in increased gold production, while residues and plant lockup were expected to reduce steadily. Certain contributory design deficiencies were also attended to.</p>
<p>In addition, plant lockup of gold was also normal in the first few quarters of operation.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
